<% content_for :title, "About, Papi" %>

<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
  <h1 class="display text-[34px] tracking-tight">About</h1>

  <div class="prose mt-8">
    <p>
      Papi is an API specification tool built by Bartosz Krajka. It started as a
      question: what would OpenAPI look like with a tenth of its surface, and what
      could you add with the room left over?
    </p>
    <p>
      The answer turned out to be a review workflow, a diff that understands schemas
      instead of text, comments anchored to what a thing <em>is</em> rather than to a
      row id, and a mock server that makes a spec runnable the moment it is written.
    </p>
    <h2>How it is built</h2>
    <p>
      Rails, SQLite, Hotwire, Tailwind. No bundler and no build step for JavaScript.
      Every controller is Stimulus loaded through importmap. The schema language has
      one hand-written parser, in Ruby, serving the diff, the validator, the mock
      server and the editor alike.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
